# CMT_L: the clock crossing of the CMT/XIPHY column (X16) on the K26.
#
# prjuray-db has no CMT_L segbits: the ZU3EG's tile is CMT_RIGHT. Every K26
# BRAM column, and two thirds of the fabric, lie east of X16, so without these
# a PS clock (BUFG_PS, west edge) never reaches them: kv260_bram_rom read all
# zero on the board (2026-10-25).
#
# Characterised with designs/kv260_clk_char (Vivado, characterisation only):
# 56 specimens, each 6-12 PS clocks on LOC'd BUFG_PS_<k> (which drives
# HROUTE<k> and nothing else) into pblocked counters in random clock regions.
# Vivado always crosses as HROUTE_0_k -> CMT_MUX_2TO1_<8k+2> -> HROUTE_1_k,
# the mux nextpnr picks too. Over 224 tile instances every set bit is
# explained by these features alone.
#
# The frame-ECC halfwords (90-92, relative bits 96-143 here) are excluded:
# xcframes2bit recomputes them, bitread masks them, and they change with
# everything else in the frame. Counting them first made the CMT_L bits look
# context-dependent; they are not.
#
# Positions agree with CMT_RIGHT where it has the feature (HROUTE_1_k.USED,
# HDISTR_0_k.USED, and its !x_144 VCC-pip bit is the mux select here).
# HROUTE crossings are characterised for the PS row (CMT_L_X16Y180) only; the
# tile-relative bits are the same type-wide.
CMT_L.WIRE.CLK_HROUTE_1_0.USED.V1 add-feature 07_149
CMT_L.PIP.CLK_HROUTE_1_0.CLK_CMT_MUX_2TO1_2_CLK_OUT add-feature 07_152 07_95  # 21 specimens
CMT_L.WIRE.CLK_HDISTR_0_0.USED.V1 add-feature 07_33  # 14 instances
CMT_L.WIRE.CLK_HROUTE_1_1.USED.V1 add-feature 06_149
CMT_L.PIP.CLK_HROUTE_1_1.CLK_CMT_MUX_2TO1_10_CLK_OUT add-feature 06_152 06_95  # 13 specimens
CMT_L.WIRE.CLK_HDISTR_0_1.USED.V1 add-feature 06_33  # 8 instances
CMT_L.WIRE.CLK_HROUTE_1_2.USED.V1 add-feature 07_150
CMT_L.PIP.CLK_HROUTE_1_2.CLK_CMT_MUX_2TO1_18_CLK_OUT add-feature 07_144 07_153  # 25 specimens
CMT_L.WIRE.CLK_HDISTR_0_2.USED.V1 add-feature 07_34  # 13 instances
CMT_L.WIRE.CLK_HROUTE_1_3.USED.V1 add-feature 06_150
